From cb0261062f5556edfcf6b3e5bf944b4278e858db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:36:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(migrate): land beads activity events + interactions in
 kernel_events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

forge migrate --from beads now transfers the full legacy activity log — every
events.jsonl lifecycle event (2378 in the real corpus) and interactions.jsonl
agent interaction/memory record (34) — into the kernel_events table
(namespaced beads.event.* / beads.interaction.*, origin=beads_import),
preserving each record's kind, actor, timestamp and payload. The write is
idempotent (deterministic id + ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) so re-migration mints no
duplicates, and needs NO schema change (kernel_events already fits).

Issue-level field gaps are resolved onto existing columns: beads owner →
assignee (falling back after an explicit assignee, else retained under
metadata.beads_owner), and design/assignee now land on their kernel columns
instead of being dropped. The spurious empty-"{}" dependencies.metadata gap is
dropped. Gaps fall 7 → 1: only dependencies.created_by remains, kept as a
documented gap (no kernel_dependencies creator column).

Dry-run/import summaries now surface an events count. Regenerated the D20 bd
call-site kill-list artifact (line-number shifts only; counts unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
